{
  "protocol": {
    "scope": "Five-fold whole-clip out-of-fold development at four previously examined PINNS sites. Official annotated positions/typed IDs for ego and neighbors; this is an oracle-tracking feature experiment on previously seen locations. No neural model, maps, pose, fixed/moving label, scene ID or image input. No test-set tuning.",
    "windows": "Disjoint complete 35-frame blocks per clip/person at 10 Hz. Five past points span 0.4 s. Score 30 future steps through +3 s. Neighbor absence never removes a window. Synchronized clips or the same person across different clip IDs cannot be identified from these public annotations.",
    "folds": "Same five previously frozen, site-stratified whole-clip folds as the action probes. Assignments depend only on site, clip name and window count. No event or residual enters allocation.",
    "features": "Motion: eight ground coordinates of the first four observations relative to the fifth. For each of Person and Car within 10 m inclusive of ego at t0, availability adds log(1+count), presence and usable nearest-neighbor velocity. Nearest ranks use t0 distance then lowest numeric ID. Geometry adds nearest dx,dy,distance,dvx,dvy,closing speed. Relative velocity subtracts ego five-point OLS from the neighbor's OLS over its available points within those same five frames (minimum two points); positive closing means approaching. Missing entries and coincident-position radial speed are zero, with channel masks as above. All features in calibrated world axes. Actor classes and IDs are annotated.",
    "fit": "CV uses the OLS velocity from five observed ego points. All three ridge models directly predict 30 xy residuals to that same CV. Warm-start, fitting on held-out clips, tuning, reweighting and clipping are absent. Training-only population standardization (SD <=1e-10 uses divisor 1), training mean residual as unpenalized intercept. Per coordinate, mean squared error plus 0.1 times squared coefficient norm; deterministic direct solve.",
    "primary": "Motion + availability + geometry minus motion-only ridge, equal-weighting four fixed sites after window-weighted means within each site. ADE is primary; FDE and geometry increment over availability are secondary. Negative is less error. Report all OOF windows and prespecified neighbor-presence strata.",
    "interpretation": "Neighbor counts, directions and distances may proxy site or traffic patterns. Differences cannot establish a causal social response. Each ridge is fitted separately, so its predictions can differ even on windows with no measured neighbor.",
    "interval": "95% percentile intervals on paired primary ADE/FDE. With PCG64 seed 2026, jointly resample whole clips with replacement 20,000 times within each of the four fixed sites, preserving all clip windows; average the four site means equally. Conditional on realized OOF fits; shared training folds and possible cross-clip dependence are not modeled. Descriptive development uncertainty, not out-of-site generalization."
  },
